# Git remotes (Ensemble v2)

This repo has **two GitHub remotes**. Pushes must go to the **team org repo**, not only the personal fork.

## Remotes

| Remote | URL | Use |
|--------|-----|-----|
| **`ensemble`** | `https://github.com/Ensemble-Digital-Labs/ensmeblewebsite.git` | **Canonical team repo** — push here so the team sees changes |
| **`origin`** | `https://github.com/giachinh1/ensemblev2.git` | Personal fork — optional backup |

## Push commands

When the user asks to push to GitHub:

```bash
# staging (primary dev branch)
git push ensemble staging

# main
git push ensemble main
```

**Do not** push only to `origin` unless the user explicitly asks for the fork.

After pushing, confirm on:
`https://github.com/Ensemble-Digital-Labs/ensmeblewebsite/tree/<branch>`

## Branch tracking

- `staging` may track `origin/staging` or `ensemble/staging` depending on last push — always push to **`ensemble`** for team visibility.
- `main` may track `ensemble/main`.

## Notes

- Org repo name is spelled **`ensmeblewebsite`** (typo in remote URL — do not “fix”).
- If the user says they don’t see commits on GitHub, check whether the push went to `origin` instead of `ensemble`.
